WEBVTT

00:00:02.848 --> 00:00:05.184
Someone has entered the Area?

00:00:05.434 --> 00:00:07.353
Did they go over Aimoto Dam?

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.525
It was opened briefly?
Where did you get that from?

00:00:15.361 --> 00:00:17.112
The Matter Defense server?

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:21.700
But Nanbara said nobody can get in.

00:00:22.034 --> 00:00:23.953
Just talking to myself.

00:00:24.703 --> 00:00:26.580
Sorry for the trouble.

00:00:26.705 --> 00:00:31.085
I know. Yes, I know very well. Good night.

00:00:32.544 --> 00:00:34.129
There isn't much I can do.

00:00:35.297 --> 00:00:38.050
Yuya and the rest
just left Yanagawara Camp,

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.969
so I can't contact them.

00:00:44.974 --> 00:00:46.392
Yes!

00:00:47.977 --> 00:00:49.770
You silly Matter!

00:00:50.354 --> 00:00:53.315
This is a competition!
You have to try harder!

00:00:55.192 --> 00:00:57.444
Kaede! Don't assume Evidence is right!

00:00:58.112 --> 00:00:59.446
Yeah, I know!

00:01:02.783 --> 00:01:07.162
She sure is having fun.
She's forgotten she's the diversion.

00:01:08.831 --> 00:01:12.501
I'm getting sick of facing
the same damn stuff all the time!

00:01:12.584 --> 00:01:13.460
Misawa!

00:01:14.128 --> 00:01:15.004
Kaede!

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:28.767
Crap!

00:01:29.435 --> 00:01:30.352
Damn it!

00:03:20.045 --> 00:03:22.131
Enough of you
getting carried away!

00:03:23.298 --> 00:03:25.509
Your job is to distract the Matter,

00:03:25.718 --> 00:03:27.970
not to put the Beetle in danger.
Damn it!

00:03:29.096 --> 00:03:31.432
Just going on strolls with the client

00:03:31.515 --> 00:03:33.934
won't score you any points either, right?

00:03:34.059 --> 00:03:34.977
I'm sorry.

00:03:35.936 --> 00:03:40.065
It's my fault for not supplying Kaede
with effective information.

00:03:40.149 --> 00:03:43.235
We'd never seen that kind of
Matter variation before!

00:03:43.318 --> 00:03:44.653
We couldn't have known...

00:03:44.737 --> 00:03:47.614
I knew Kaede would show off.

00:03:48.198 --> 00:03:51.493
As her partner,
I should have controlled her better.

00:03:51.785 --> 00:03:55.122
Which means
you're still an inexperienced team.

00:03:59.293 --> 00:04:00.586
This is bad.

00:04:01.170 --> 00:04:05.424
The Matter has entered the actuator
and crystallized.

00:04:06.008 --> 00:04:08.886
It's going to take a while to get it out.

00:04:09.344 --> 00:04:10.637
Will it be all right?

00:04:11.221 --> 00:04:13.140
At sunrise tomorrow,

00:04:13.223 --> 00:04:16.059
the Matter around K2 will become active.

00:04:16.143 --> 00:04:17.644
Judging from the timing,

00:04:17.811 --> 00:04:20.314
activity around the gate
will last a week.

00:04:20.856 --> 00:04:24.276
If we get stopped for that long,
we'll run out of time.

00:04:24.777 --> 00:04:26.361
-I'll hurry.
-All right.

00:04:26.612 --> 00:04:28.822
I'll watch the Matter on the river.

00:04:29.865 --> 00:04:31.241
What's up with her?

00:04:31.742 --> 00:04:33.535
I have a favor to ask, Minase.

00:04:33.911 --> 00:04:34.745
What is it?

00:04:39.291 --> 00:04:41.418
I'm going to Misawa and Seri.

00:04:42.461 --> 00:04:43.337
Why?

00:04:43.921 --> 00:04:45.422
I want to thank them.

00:04:46.048 --> 00:04:48.383
They're working hard to protect us.

00:04:49.259 --> 00:04:50.177
Stay here.

00:04:50.594 --> 00:04:52.304
If you put yourself in danger

00:04:52.387 --> 00:04:54.807
and cause more trouble, there's no point.

00:05:07.694 --> 00:05:08.737
Kazuki!

00:05:09.488 --> 00:05:11.657
Aiko, are you all right?

00:05:12.241 --> 00:05:15.911
I'm more worried about Misawa and Seri.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:17.955
They'll get what they deserve.

00:05:18.372 --> 00:05:19.206
Hey!

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:24.086
It's a sample of the crystallized Matter.

00:05:24.711 --> 00:05:26.171
I heard from Shinoyama

00:05:26.463 --> 00:05:30.259
that you're chemically synthesizing
vial cartridges on the fly.

00:05:30.342 --> 00:05:31.635
Are you serious?

00:05:32.135 --> 00:05:33.595
Chemical synthesis?

00:05:34.179 --> 00:05:36.265
That's how cartridges are prepared.

00:05:36.848 --> 00:05:39.476
If we can't deliver
this new data to Town,

00:05:40.352 --> 00:05:42.145
we have to synthesize it here.

00:05:42.729 --> 00:05:44.189
Who the hell are you?

00:05:44.398 --> 00:05:47.568
Aren't you supposed
to not get involved with clients?

00:05:57.911 --> 00:06:01.748
That guy really annoys me!
Who the hell does he think he is?

00:06:01.832 --> 00:06:03.542
He even involved you, Haruka!

00:06:04.334 --> 00:06:07.462
I only apologized for my own mistakes.

00:06:07.546 --> 00:06:09.506
You didn't do anything wrong!

00:06:10.591 --> 00:06:13.010
When this is over
and we return to Town,

00:06:13.802 --> 00:06:15.762
you should partner with better people.

00:06:16.471 --> 00:06:18.557
Is that what you want, Kaede?

00:06:22.102 --> 00:06:23.186
<i>If this keeps up,</i>

00:06:23.812 --> 00:06:26.231
she'll trip herself up someday for sure.

00:06:27.232 --> 00:06:30.152
That's all part of our evaluation.

00:06:30.402 --> 00:06:31.320
Damn it!

00:06:32.654 --> 00:06:37.659
If that Kanzaki wasn't our client,
I would never work with that jerk!

00:06:38.243 --> 00:06:40.621
Dream contact?

00:06:41.622 --> 00:06:46.835
That's when your brain links with
your other brain located at Primary Point.

00:06:47.502 --> 00:06:51.340
Information from the other you
is transmitted like a dream.

00:06:51.965 --> 00:06:53.842
By observing those dreams,

00:06:54.134 --> 00:06:56.929
I can see what's happening
at Primary Point.

00:06:57.971 --> 00:06:59.598
The other me?

00:07:00.182 --> 00:07:01.141
Don't worry.

00:07:01.892 --> 00:07:05.604
You have already experienced this
several times while sleeping.

00:07:06.396 --> 00:07:10.108
You've seen
how your mother and brother are doing now

00:07:10.442 --> 00:07:12.069
in your dreams, right?

00:07:12.402 --> 00:07:14.696
That's part of this Dream Contact.

00:07:15.697 --> 00:07:16.573
I see.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:20.661
Those dreams are what
the other me is seeing.

00:07:21.411 --> 00:07:22.245
However,

00:07:22.871 --> 00:07:27.125
until now, these contacts
have been coincidental and passive.

00:07:28.085 --> 00:07:29.211
This time,

00:07:29.544 --> 00:07:31.880
we will be using
the Beetle's processing unit

00:07:32.172 --> 00:07:36.218
to make a more precise and active contact.

00:07:40.764 --> 00:07:42.599
My brain was copied,

00:07:43.141 --> 00:07:48.105
and there is another Aiko Tachibana
with the same memories as me.

00:07:49.314 --> 00:07:50.691
I wonder how she feels.

00:07:53.235 --> 00:07:55.070
What? Wait a second!

00:07:55.153 --> 00:07:57.614
You've been observing my dreams?

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:00.117
By what right?
How could you?

00:08:01.284 --> 00:08:02.577
Those are my dreams!

00:08:02.661 --> 00:08:06.123
If I knew you were going to
observe my dreams,

00:08:06.248 --> 00:08:09.209
I would've tried
not to have embarrassing ones!

00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:11.169
I'm calling them dreams,

00:08:11.503 --> 00:08:14.631
but they are only thoughts
from the other you.

00:08:17.551 --> 00:08:18.802
Do you get it?

00:08:18.885 --> 00:08:21.888
There are other people
that must be placated.

00:08:22.264 --> 00:08:23.724
The Matter eradication wing?

00:08:23.807 --> 00:08:28.311
And abroad. This affects the economy,
internal affairs, and national security.

00:08:28.395 --> 00:08:29.771
The government will use

00:08:29.855 --> 00:08:32.691
destruction of the Area
to bargain, if necessary.

00:08:33.233 --> 00:08:36.111
To protect Japan's
artificial organism industry,

00:08:36.194 --> 00:08:37.946
we need an ace up our sleeve.

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:38.864
For example,

00:08:39.489 --> 00:08:42.159
showing the world that we've
already achieved

00:08:42.367 --> 00:08:45.245
a new advancement in artificial organisms.

00:08:46.580 --> 00:08:49.124
You'd have us expose
the advantage we have?

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.210
If people know the size of the fish,

00:08:52.294 --> 00:08:54.379
we can't expect them to keep quiet.

00:08:55.255 --> 00:08:59.426
In order to accomplish this,
Aiko Tachibana, our greatest achievement,

00:08:59.885 --> 00:09:02.179
must not be lost.

00:09:02.763 --> 00:09:06.266
Unbelievable.
You've got a hell of a lot of guts.

00:09:06.558 --> 00:09:07.601
Of course I do.

00:09:08.226 --> 00:09:12.355
If Toshihide Yura were still around,
this may not have been necessary.

00:09:13.398 --> 00:09:14.608
He is already dead!

00:09:17.861 --> 00:09:21.573
Yura is gone. And there is
no such thing as the Yura Notes.

00:09:22.074 --> 00:09:26.203
That is exactly why
I will bring back Aiko Tachibana,

00:09:27.245 --> 00:09:29.247
no matter what it takes.

00:09:31.666 --> 00:09:35.003
<i>I can't let this end now.</i>

00:09:47.849 --> 00:09:49.684
SCHOOL ORIENTATION CEREMONY

00:10:04.074 --> 00:10:05.117
MUSIC COMPETITION

00:10:06.284 --> 00:10:08.453
<i> What is this?</i>

00:10:09.287 --> 00:10:11.540
<i>What in the world is all this?</i>

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.721
Kanzaki.

00:10:29.432 --> 00:10:33.854
I saw Mom and Ryota again.
And Dr. Yura, too.

00:10:35.647 --> 00:10:38.692
You must know Dr. Yura, right, Kanzaki?

00:10:40.026 --> 00:10:42.320
Toshihide Yura...

00:10:42.904 --> 00:10:43.738
I thought so.

00:10:44.072 --> 00:10:45.448
Dad even said,

00:10:46.658 --> 00:10:50.078
"He's young,
but he's a very famous researcher."

00:10:51.121 --> 00:10:55.208
But the Dr. Yura
that I knew wasn't like that.

00:10:55.917 --> 00:10:59.004
He was rather elusive and mysterious.

00:11:00.755 --> 00:11:02.257
That's strange.

00:11:02.841 --> 00:11:06.845
I never saw Dr. Yura outdoors
under a blue sky like that.

00:11:07.846 --> 00:11:11.808
I only met him at the checkups
Dad's company did at Kiryu Hospital,

00:11:11.892 --> 00:11:14.185
and at the surgery after the accident.

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:16.396
Is that a dream

00:11:17.439 --> 00:11:18.523
from the other me?

00:11:18.899 --> 00:11:22.652
It seemed like the memories
of a different person.

00:11:24.529 --> 00:11:25.614
You must be tired.

00:11:26.031 --> 00:11:29.034
The mingling of consciousness
during Dream Contact

00:11:29.242 --> 00:11:30.702
is hard on the brain.

00:11:31.369 --> 00:11:33.038
You should rest for a while.

00:11:33.663 --> 00:11:36.041
No, I can't rest.

00:11:36.708 --> 00:11:37.542
Because,

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:40.128
<i>everyone is working so hard.</i>

00:11:40.503 --> 00:11:42.505
<i>I have to work even harder.</i>

00:11:44.633 --> 00:11:47.177
There must be something I can do.

00:11:50.388 --> 00:11:51.222
Gummi!

00:11:56.603 --> 00:11:58.939
You must've been hungry. Sorry.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:04.486
Is that good?

00:12:06.446 --> 00:12:10.909
So, even your brain is
an artificial organism, right?

00:12:11.034 --> 00:12:15.163
What are you thinking? What is it like?

00:12:16.998 --> 00:12:20.460
But you know,
those rations don't have any taste at all.

00:12:20.961 --> 00:12:21.920
I have an idea!

00:12:23.964 --> 00:12:26.091
Okay, we're ready to go.

00:12:27.509 --> 00:12:28.426
Shiraishi!

00:12:31.554 --> 00:12:33.890
<i>To get inside Area Three,</i>

00:12:33.974 --> 00:12:38.561
<i>we absolutely must arrive at K2</i>
<i>before sunrise tomorrow.</i>

00:12:38.937 --> 00:12:41.439
<i>Everyone must keep that in mind!</i>

00:12:42.774 --> 00:12:44.651
If I rehydrate this package,

00:12:45.235 --> 00:12:47.153
it will be like mashed potatoes.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:50.156
Then, I can add some heated chicken

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:54.244
She's trying to raise morale
by making the meals delicious.

00:12:54.703 --> 00:12:57.080
All they need is nutrition and calories.

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:59.249
Forget about it. Sit back down.

00:12:59.833 --> 00:13:00.750
But...

00:13:02.168 --> 00:13:04.796
Hey! Don't do that!

00:13:08.842 --> 00:13:11.970
This is odd.
It feels like something's coming.

00:13:14.472 --> 00:13:15.890
Malignant!

00:13:21.438 --> 00:13:22.689
Evidence!

00:13:22.814 --> 00:13:24.607
Golf 24 Iota!

00:13:24.858 --> 00:13:26.860
The mutations still keep coming.

00:13:27.235 --> 00:13:28.611
Area Two positions!

00:13:28.695 --> 00:13:30.864
Misawa and Seri, divert the Matter!

00:13:31.281 --> 00:13:33.199
<i>Sagami and Minase, guard the Beetle!</i>

00:13:33.908 --> 00:13:35.285
What is that?

00:13:35.618 --> 00:13:36.786
A Matter ceiling.

00:13:37.203 --> 00:13:39.914
It's okay.
That Matter has always been dormant.

00:13:39.998 --> 00:13:40.874
Wait!

00:13:41.041 --> 00:13:42.876
It's active!

00:13:42.959 --> 00:13:44.085
-What?
-What?

00:13:46.463 --> 00:13:48.423
We're flanked above and below.

00:13:49.007 --> 00:13:50.842
Don't stop! Charge through!

00:13:51.176 --> 00:13:53.470
We have to knock out whatever we can!

00:13:53.553 --> 00:13:56.514
Remember, this isn't your one-man show.

00:13:57.557 --> 00:13:58.767
Mind your business!

00:14:16.534 --> 00:14:18.286
It's not crystallizing!

00:14:18.703 --> 00:14:20.663
This mutation is different from before.

00:14:20.747 --> 00:14:22.290
Is it a new type?

00:14:27.295 --> 00:14:29.714
-I'll hit it from the ceiling!
-Roger!

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.560
Watch out for other activity!

00:14:53.113 --> 00:14:54.280
If this keeps up,

00:14:54.364 --> 00:14:57.117
it'll attack the Beetle before long.

00:14:57.826 --> 00:14:59.202
I'll man the heavy laser.

00:14:59.285 --> 00:15:00.120
Roger.

00:15:00.495 --> 00:15:02.288
I'll link the fire assist computer.

00:15:04.332 --> 00:15:07.752
Focus on an object to target it,
then pull the trigger.

00:15:07.877 --> 00:15:08.711
Got it?

00:15:08.962 --> 00:15:11.214
And this adjusts power and wavelength.

00:15:11.297 --> 00:15:12.674
Here it comes again!

00:15:13.258 --> 00:15:15.635
-Aiko?
-It's coming! From over there!

00:15:23.226 --> 00:15:24.102
Over there!

00:15:28.356 --> 00:15:30.483
-How can you tell?
-I don't know!

00:15:31.067 --> 00:15:33.528
How come? How can I tell?

00:15:34.028 --> 00:15:37.282
The laser's vial cartridge
and Evidence aren't right!

00:15:37.365 --> 00:15:39.534
None of our weapons are effective!

00:15:39.617 --> 00:15:43.037
If nothing is effective,
we may as well give up!

00:15:45.999 --> 00:15:47.584
I know! I'll get a sample!

00:15:48.126 --> 00:15:50.295
I need a piece of Matter we've shot.

00:15:51.087 --> 00:15:52.005
There's one!

00:16:03.892 --> 00:16:04.851
Got it!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:24.954
Chemically synthesize this, Yuya Kanzaki!

00:16:27.457 --> 00:16:28.541
Got it!

00:16:30.877 --> 00:16:32.837
I'll take over the laser cannon.

00:16:32.921 --> 00:16:34.547
-What?
-Sit still!

00:16:34.631 --> 00:16:37.425
That is your most important job!

00:16:42.597 --> 00:16:44.516
I can't just sit still!

00:16:46.476 --> 00:16:47.560
Shiraishi!

00:16:47.644 --> 00:16:49.938
Patch me into everyone!

00:16:53.274 --> 00:16:54.776
Sagami, above you!

00:16:58.446 --> 00:16:59.697
Thanks for that!

00:16:59.781 --> 00:17:01.115
Haruka, behind you!

00:17:02.575 --> 00:17:03.952
How did you know?

00:17:04.035 --> 00:17:05.328
Shinoyama, there!

00:17:06.663 --> 00:17:07.539
Kaede!

00:17:09.916 --> 00:17:12.335
I like it! This is getting interesting!

00:17:12.919 --> 00:17:15.338
I'll kick your butt now!

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:17.632
Don't attack it alone, Kaede!

00:17:17.715 --> 00:17:22.345
But it's my fault
that we have to make up time!

00:17:24.305 --> 00:17:25.348
It's active!

00:17:36.276 --> 00:17:38.486
This isn't your one-man show.

00:17:39.237 --> 00:17:42.991
I can't help it.
This is how I've always done things.

00:17:54.002 --> 00:17:57.338
Excellent! Now, just hold still!

00:17:57.922 --> 00:17:58.756
Kaede!

00:18:00.675 --> 00:18:03.303
What? Why didn't you leave me?

00:18:03.386 --> 00:18:05.054
I won't disgrace my name

00:18:05.346 --> 00:18:07.515
by letting one of my comrades die!

00:18:09.601 --> 00:18:10.727
It's completed!

00:18:13.396 --> 00:18:15.898
<i>Cartridges loaded</i>
<i>onto an automated bipod!</i>

00:18:16.232 --> 00:18:17.817
Roger! Let's go!

00:18:17.942 --> 00:18:18.943
All right!

00:18:21.279 --> 00:18:23.990
I'll stay alive! Will that satisfy you?

00:18:25.366 --> 00:18:26.826
That's the spirit!

00:18:28.536 --> 00:18:31.706
-Your arm!
-It's artificial anyway.

00:18:36.461 --> 00:18:38.796
-It's crystallizing!
-Perfect!

00:18:45.845 --> 00:18:46.846
Amazing!

00:18:46.929 --> 00:18:48.765
They're all coming at the same time!

00:19:14.791 --> 00:19:15.708
-Yes!
-Yes!

00:19:16.292 --> 00:19:17.126
We did it!

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:19.003
Wait, Aiko?

00:19:20.171 --> 00:19:22.006
-Tachibana!
-Aiko!

00:19:25.093 --> 00:19:26.094
Are you okay?

00:19:26.177 --> 00:19:27.387
It's over.

00:19:28.638 --> 00:19:30.056
Thank goodness.

00:19:48.199 --> 00:19:49.033
What?

00:19:49.117 --> 00:19:51.661
You have been dismissed.

00:19:52.620 --> 00:19:56.958
It was a unanimous vote by the board
of directors, except for you.

00:19:57.542 --> 00:20:00.169
I've been fired? Why?

00:20:01.504 --> 00:20:03.297
Certainly, you must know why.

00:20:03.881 --> 00:20:06.926
I can think of many reasons.
Which one was it?

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:12.140
With your use of funds
from Dr. Kiryu's research budget,

00:20:12.724 --> 00:20:14.642
we discovered falsified records.

00:20:15.268 --> 00:20:16.728
What about Dr. Kiryu?

00:20:17.562 --> 00:20:21.107
<i>He defended you by saying its use was</i>
<i>at your discretion.</i>

00:20:21.691 --> 00:20:25.528
<i>But we couldn't possibly ignore</i>
<i>the infraction of company rules</i>

00:20:25.987 --> 00:20:27.864
<i>in the accounting report.</i>

00:20:30.324 --> 00:20:31.284
Too bad.

00:20:33.661 --> 00:20:34.871
I messed up!

00:20:34.954 --> 00:20:37.665
With me out of the way,
nobody will block

00:20:37.749 --> 00:20:39.459
whoever is running Kiryu Research.

00:20:40.126 --> 00:20:42.670
The problem now is the old man's password.

00:20:43.421 --> 00:20:46.048
<i>Those files are still on the server.</i>

00:20:46.799 --> 00:20:48.301
<i>If that stuff gets out...</i>

00:20:53.431 --> 00:20:57.393
I didn't expect your chemical synthesis
would come in handy.

00:20:57.852 --> 00:21:00.980
It was thanks to the data you collected.

00:21:01.731 --> 00:21:05.443
You even made me a new arm.
Who the hell are you?

00:21:06.027 --> 00:21:07.653
-How's it going?
-All done.

00:21:09.030 --> 00:21:11.699
How did you know
where the Matter was coming from?

00:21:12.283 --> 00:21:14.202
I'm wondering, too.

00:21:14.285 --> 00:21:16.954
Who cares about that? We won!

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:20.166
And you made our rations taste great!

00:21:20.249 --> 00:21:21.709
Way to go, Aiko!

00:21:22.460 --> 00:21:24.545
You're right! This looks great!

00:21:26.172 --> 00:21:28.841
She senses Matter,
but loses consciousness.

00:21:28.966 --> 00:21:31.302
It must be the active Dream Contact.

00:21:31.636 --> 00:21:32.637
Is that possible?

00:21:32.845 --> 00:21:34.555
It's highly probable.

00:21:35.389 --> 00:21:37.350
Something else bothers me.

00:21:38.559 --> 00:21:40.061
It appears the other Aiko

00:21:40.311 --> 00:21:44.106
at Primary Point is losing consciousness.

00:21:44.190 --> 00:21:45.149
Really?

00:21:45.525 --> 00:21:48.110
It's likely due
to all the recent activity.

00:21:48.194 --> 00:21:50.238
If we don't hurry,

00:21:50.321 --> 00:21:52.949
she may lose consciousness
before we arrive.

00:21:53.407 --> 00:21:55.701
If she does,
the surgery won't be possible.

00:21:58.996 --> 00:22:01.082
-What?
-What's wrong?

00:22:07.880 --> 00:22:08.714
<i>Malignant!</i>

00:22:08.798 --> 00:22:10.591
Everyone, prepare for action!

00:22:13.761 --> 00:22:16.722
Wait! There's something
on the close-range sensor!

00:22:17.557 --> 00:22:19.850
Heat source at five o'clock!

00:23:57.823 --> 00:23:59.909
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
